\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The cut and the termination of a Shakti array set the boundary of its domino tiling. (a)~Islands (bars) and plaquettes, H in orange and V in blue. In a ground state each plaquette shares one unhappy vertex (dot) with a perpendicular neighbor, which makes the pair a dimer. Red bar: the stem island of one plaquette. (b)~Slope square of the height function. Its corners are the four ice phases; a through-block axis cut fixes one component of the slope (an edge of the square, squares), and an even $45^\circ $ cut fixes the whole slope (a corner, dots). (c)~Ground state of a corner switch ($L=12$): the west and south edges are block-aligned, the north and east edges are cut through the blocks with fringed termination. Plaquettes without their stem island are free (yellow) and gain $J/2$. Half-dimer sites (diamonds) are boundary vertices that can become unhappy while covering a single plaquette, at a cost of $J/2$; they matter only at $T>0$.}}{3}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:cuts}{{1}{3}{The cut and the termination of a Shakti array set the boundary of its domino tiling. (a)~Islands (bars) and plaquettes, H in orange and V in blue. In a ground state each plaquette shares one unhappy vertex (dot) with a perpendicular neighbor, which makes the pair a dimer. Red bar: the stem island of one plaquette. (b)~Slope square of the height function. Its corners are the four ice phases; a through-block axis cut fixes one component of the slope (an edge of the square, squares), and an even $45^\circ $ cut fixes the whole slope (a corner, dots). (c)~Ground state of a corner switch ($L=12$): the west and south edges are block-aligned, the north and east edges are cut through the blocks with fringed termination. Plaquettes without their stem island are free (yellow) and gain $J/2$. Half-dimer sites (diamonds) are boundary vertices that can become unhappy while covering a single plaquette, at a cost of $J/2$; they matter only at $T>0$}{figure.1}{}}
\newlabel{eq:D2}{{2}{3}{}{equation.2.2}{}}
